+ *
+ * Same rows as viewbench over logos_view_*_i32, verified against qsort, and the same two paired
+ * comparisons for the quantile batch. The shapes are chosen for what the int32 dispatcher does with
+ * them: span 1e8 and the full int32 range reach the histogram partition and defer the leaf; span 2e5
+ * fits the counting route's table (2^18 slots), which sorts the array outright, so the view holds one
+ * finished bucket and the prediction is NO gain there; clustered ints (16 clusters 1e5 wide, 1e8 apart)
+ * partition with unequal buckets.
+ *
+ * Usage: ./viewbench_i32 [reps] [n] [pairs]                        LOGOS_THREADS=N overrides. */
+#define _GNU_SOURCE
+#include "logos_psort.h"
